# Backend origin the typed API client (src/lib/env.ts) reads at build/dev
# time. This is the URL the *browser* sends requests to — it is NOT the same
# thing as the page's own origin, which is what the backend's CORS allow-list
# checks (backend/settings.py CORS_ORIGINS).
#
# Cross-origin arithmetic (counter-intuitive, breaks silently if ignored):
#   - Browsing to http://localhost:5173 (Vite's default dev port, and the
#     first entry in the backend's default CORS_ORIGINS) while this var
#     points at http://127.0.0.1:8000 WORKS — the page origin is allow-listed.
#   - Browsing to http://127.0.0.1:5173 instead does NOT work, even though
#     it's the same machine — that page origin is absent from the backend's
#     default CORS_ORIGINS allow-list. The fix is to add it to the backend's
#     CORS_ORIGINS, not to change this variable.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
